NAME
       webscan - look for pages a web site doesn't link to (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       webscan [-w WORDLIST] http://HOST[:PORT]/[FOLDER/]

DESCRIPTION
       webscan asks the web server for a list of common page and folder names
       (default /usr/share/wordlists/range-paths.txt) and reports the ones that
       exist (any answer but 404 Not Found). Forgotten admin pages, backups and
       test folders are often found this way. Every request lands in the web
       server's log, so it is noisy.

       Also look at robots.txt: it lists pages a site asks search engines not
       to show, which tells visitors where to look.

OPTIONS
       -w WORDLIST   the names to try, one on each line

EXAMPLES
       webscan http://10.10.1.40/
       curl http://10.10.1.40/robots.txt

SEE ALSO
       curl(1), nmap(1), vulnlookup(1)
